  ],
  "forward_vector": "I am the manifest of Kuramoto Coupling's rich face: what the Shop gathered and made for each section, and the fingerprint of the words each piece was made against, so the page can say when a piece may lag the text. I grow when the entry is enriched again; I never hold the entry's words.",
  "entry": "Kuramoto Coupling",
  "tier": "study",
  "made": "2026-09-24",
  "round": 1,
  "page": {
    "bed": {
      "file": "opening-bed.wav",
      "volume": 0.14
    }
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Kuramoto Coupling",
      "made_against": "2df4c71c56ee",
      "made": "2026-09-24",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "file": "intro-narration.wav",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "intro narration · Kokoro, af_heart",
          "caption": "The first line of the Shop's Round 1 reel, spoken: *how populations of oscillators find a shared rhythm.*",
          "near": "The Kuramoto model describes"
        },
        {
          "file": "Kuramoto Coupling — rich — equation.md",
          "origin": "made",
          "by": "the Maker · typeset",
          "caption": "The model in one line, then the crowd's togetherness — each shown twice, in symbols and in words.",
          "near": "The coupling constant"
        },
        {
          "file": "two-phasors-uncoupled-manim.mp4",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "two phasors, uncoupled · Manim",
          "caption": "**Two phasors, uncoupled** — a Sketch-tier teaching artifact for the sub-threshold case. Indigo at 1.00 Hz, amber at 1.07 Hz, free-running. They begin in phase, drift apart by the close-but-detectable frequency gap, and never re-align. This is K = 0: independence, no cooperation."
        },
        {
          "file": "uncoupled-narration.wav",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "narration for the uncoupled phasors · Kokoro",
          "caption": "The voice-over this clip was cut to in the Round 1 reel.",
          "place": "band"
        },
        {
          "file": "two-phasors-uncoupled-matplotlib.mp4",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "two phasors, uncoupled · Matplotlib",
          "caption": "The same scene in Matplotlib — kept because the Cowork-era sandbox forced a non-canonical render that turned out to have its own visual character worth holding.",
          "place": "margin"
        },
        {
          "file": "two-phasors-coupling-explorer.html",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "height": 790,
          "title": "two-phasor coupling explorer · p5.js",
          "caption": "**Couple the two phasors and find K_c yourself.** The same two oscillators, but K is now a slider. Critical coupling for this pair is K_c ≈ 0.220 — drag the slider across that threshold and watch the two go from drift to lock. The order parameter R is the small vector in the middle: |R| → 1 is the formal signature of synchrony."
        },
        {
          "file": "two-oscillators-coupling-explorer-audio.html",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "height": 730,
          "title": "two-oscillator audio coupling explorer · Tone.js",
          "caption": "**Hear it too.** The same two oscillators, audio-rate. Beating envelope at low K; lock above K_c. The visual explorer asked you to *see* the threshold — this one asks you to *hear* it. Same dynamics, different sense."
        }
      ],
      "stamped": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "heading": "The Fine-Tuning Insight",
      "made_against": "b99e3ec8deae",
      "made": "2026-09-24",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "file": "Kuramoto Coupling — rich — waveform-locking.html",
          "origin": "made",
          "height": 920,
          "by": "Web Audio Worklet",
          "caption": "**Path B, heard.** The claim above, made audible and checked: a saw driver pulls its follower onto a true octave; a square wave, with no second harmonic, cannot — but it can lock the twelfth. The lock thresholds match K ≥ 2|Δf| ⁄ bₘ.",
          "near": "Path B — Nonlinear waveform coupling"
        }
      ],
      "stamped": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Cross-Domain Mirrors",
      "made_against": "16c1faa56fc3",
      "made": "2026-10-13",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "file": "fireflies-pond.png",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "fireflies over a forest pond at dusk · SDXL",
          "caption": "Fireflies over a forest pond at dusk — the first natural image people reach for when they want to feel coupled oscillators. SDXL render at the Kuramoto arc's indigo / amber palette.",
          "near": "This concept appears everywhere once you see it"
        },
        {
          "file": "phenomena-walk.mp4",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "phenomena walk · Remotion",
          "caption": "**Walk through the mirrors.** A titled card walk through four domains where the same dynamics appear: fireflies, neurons, jazz bassist, tidal friction. Each card names what plays the role of K in that domain.",
          "near": "This concept appears everywhere once you see it"
        },
        {
          "file": "speech-rhythm-and-groove-narration.wav",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "speech rhythm and groove, read aloud · Kokoro, af_heart",
          "caption": "The paragraph above, read aloud.",
          "near": "Speech rhythm and groove coupling",
          "place": "band"
        },
        {
          "file": "sync-arriving.mp4",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "sync arriving · Manim",
          "caption": "**Sync arriving.** Eight oscillators with slightly different natural frequencies; K ramps from zero across the narration. Phase arrows fade from indigo to amber as each falls into the lock; the central order-parameter vector |R| climbs from near-zero to near-one as the population coheres. The same narration above is the soundtrack — text rendered to speech (Kokoro, af_heart, −16 LUFS), speech read back to word timings (Whisper base), and the Manim scene timed against those readings. Drift over 36 s: 25 ms.",
          "near": "Speech rhythm and groove coupling"
        },
        {
          "file": "synchronization-arriving.wav",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "the sound of synchronization arriving · Stable Audio 3",
          "caption": "**The sound of synchronization arriving.** A 20-second purely auditory rendering of the same idea — scattered ticking pulses at different rates that pull into a shared rhythm and lock together. Generated by Stable Audio 3's small-sfx model. First listen on the narrative-arc question: *perhaps* — needs more study, and confirm by ear whenever SA3 is asked for time-evolving structure.",
          "near": "Speech rhythm and groove coupling",
          "place": "band"
        },
        {
          "file": "round-1-teaching-reel.mp4",
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "Round 1 teaching reel · ffmpeg",
          "caption": "**Round 1 teaching reel.** The whole arc end-to-end — two phasors uncoupled (with narration), a title-card pivot (*Now couple them*), the sync-arriving Manim+narration. Built by ffmpeg from the upstream specialist outputs; one teaching reel as the connective-tissue proof for the Shop."
        }
      ],
      "stamped": "2026-10-13"
    },
    {
      "heading": "In Our Instruments",
      "made_against": "1cee8c90d5ee",
      "made": "2026-09-24",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "file": "Kuramoto Coupling — rich — ensemble.html",
          "origin": "made",
          "height": 840,
          "by": "Web Audio Worklet",
          "caption": "**The performable boundary, in miniature.** A simpler cousin of the neurological synthesizer — one pitch cloud rather than an attractor spectrum — but the same move: K as the knob between scatter and coherence.",
          "near": "The neurological synthesizer maps this directly"
        }
      ],
      "stamped": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Asymmetric Coupling: The Stubbornness Parameter",
      "made_against": "f19f12592784",
      "made": "2026-09-24",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "file": "Kuramoto Coupling — rich — stubbornness.html",
          "origin": "made",
          "height": 900,
          "by": "Web Audio Worklet",
          "caption": "**Bright idea #38, played.** Stubbornness (K_receive → 0) sets *where* a locked crowd would settle; whether the crowd can get there takes pull (K_send) too. The settle point is every voice's pitch weighted by K_send ÷ K_receive — the simulation lands on it to the hundredth of a hertz.",
          "near": "The live performance insight"
        }
      ],
      "stamped": "2026-09-24"
    }
  ]
}
----

