{
  "title": "Language as a Tonal Medium — rich",
  "born": "2026-10-13",
  "links": [
    {
      "target": "[[Language as a Tonal Medium]]",
      "type": "connects-to",
      "label": "rich-face-of"
    },
    {
      "target": "[[Enrichment]]",
      "type": "connects-to",
      "label": "made-by"
    },
    {
      "target": "[[Semantic Webcam]]",
      "type": "connects-to",
      "label": "gathered-from"
    }
  ],
  "forward_vector": "I am the manifest of Language as a Tonal Medium's rich face: the five Semantic Webcam builds gathered beside the step of the argument each one proves, a note that fronts the camera, and the fingerprint of the words they were laid against, so the page can say when a piece may lag the text. I grow when the entry is enriched again; I never hold the entry's words.",
  "entry": "Language as a Tonal Medium",
  "tier": "sketch",
  "made": "2026-10-13",
  "round": 1,
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "The evidence — five iterations of one instrument",
      "made_against": "f9cbf285305b",
      "made": "2026-10-13",
      "pieces": [
        {
          "file": "Language as a Tonal Medium — rich — camera.md",
          "origin": "made",
          "by": "Enrichment · a note",
          "near": "The claim is not an argument"
        },
        {
          "file": "/Projects/Semantic Webcam/01-live-stigmergy-cam.html",
          "contract": {
            "needs": "camera",
            "size": "fill 4/3"
          },
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "Live STIGMERGY Cam · iteration 1",
          "caption": "**Tone only.** Your camera as an amber terminal grid: brightness picks a glyph from a density ramp, and the picture holds. Cycle the glyph sets (**g**) — blocks, CP437, ASCII, braille — and none of them ever reads. The meaning channel, absent.",
          "near": "Live STIGMERGY Cam",
          "height": 680
        },
        {
          "file": "/Projects/Semantic Webcam/02-word-flock-cam.html",
          "contract": {
            "needs": "camera",
            "size": "fill 4/3"
          },
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "Word Flock Cam · iteration 2",
          "caption": "**Meaning, unmoored.** Words flock to whatever moves and whatever is dark — a guess at your eyes and fingertips — and they say something as they go. But they ride on top of the picture instead of drawing it; the dim grid underneath still does all the shading. The failure that shows the two channels have to be joined on purpose.",
          "near": "Word Flock Cam",
          "height": 680
        },
        {
          "file": "/Projects/Semantic Webcam/03-character-multiply-cam.html",
          "contract": {
            "needs": "camera",
            "size": "fill 4/3"
          },
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "Character Multiply Cam · iteration 3, the anchor",
          "caption": "**The anchor.** Brightness picks the glyph — period, dash, a letter of a whole word, shade, then a white tile with a black letter punched into it — and whole words typeset themselves into each run of mid-tone. A region is the right darkness and a readable word at once. Press **g** to swap words for blocks: the same picture, with the reading taken out.",
          "near": "Character Multiply Cam",
          "height": 680
        },
        {
          "file": "/Projects/Semantic Webcam/04-grammar-fit-cam.html",
          "contract": {
            "needs": "camera",
            "size": "fill 4/3"
          },
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "Grammar-Fit Cam · iteration 4",
          "caption": "**The strong test.** Each blob becomes a composed line: a word-to-word chain learned from the source text walks along it, choosing what could plausibly follow and still fits the width. **w** steps flow → fill → grammar. Read a blob aloud in each and judge for yourself whether sense survives.",
          "near": "Grammar-Fit Cam",
          "height": 680
        },
        {
          "file": "/Projects/Semantic Webcam/05-tonal-word-cam.html",
          "contract": {
            "needs": "camera",
            "size": "fill 4/3"
          },
          "origin": "gathered",
          "title": "Tonal-Word Cam · iteration 5",
          "caption": "**Light picks the word.** The words hold steady under the smoothing the anchor brought in (the *smooth* slider). What this build adds: brightness now chooses *which word*, scoring each grammar-legal candidate by its ink against the blob's brightness. Sweep **b**, tone-bias, from 0, where grammar alone picks, to 1, where ink picks among the words grammar allows — the open question below, free rider or separate budget, as a slider.",
          "near": "Tonal-Word Cam",
          "height": 680
        }
      ],
      "stamped": "2026-10-13"
    }
  ]
}

